# langpack.manifest — the console half of the language profile (mod_langpack).
# Single source of truth: deploy iterates this; w-reset/drift reuse it.
# Format: <path>\t<class>   class: managed | override
#
# /etc/vconsole.conf is MACHINE STATE with two independent writers, which is why
# it is `override` (apply_rootfs excludes it once it exists) rather than managed:
#
#   • KEYMAP — chosen in the installer wizard (sys_locale) and, at every boot of
#     an encrypted machine, the layout the LUKS passphrase is typed in;
#   • FONT   — derived from the locale by `w-langpack font`, so a TTY does not
#     transliterate non-Latin text (config-i18n.md §4).
#
# rootfs/etc/vconsole.conf stays in the repo as the seed for a machine that has
# none. It shipped `KEYMAP=us` and was NOT declared here until 2026-09-10, so
# every `apply.sh --rootfs` rsynced it back over the live file — which silently
# reverted the keymap the user picked during installation, and (once w-langpack
# existed) dropped the console font on the very next apply. Found by checking
# `/etc/vconsole.conf` after a deploy rather than after the command that wrote it.
/etc/vconsole.conf	override
